module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ExceptionalCartier
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ProjectiveSpaceEmbedding
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.TwistDegreeOne
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.TwistOneIdealSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierConormal.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.DivisorPicardClass
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.NormalSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjIdealSheaf.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjMapTwistDegreeSection.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistDegreeOneCover.Basic

/-!
# The twists of the blowup of an affine scheme, and the sheaves of its exceptional divisor

Let `R` be a commutative ring and `I ⊆ R` an ideal generated by `x₀, …, x_{m-1}`. The Rees
presentation of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/ProjectiveSpaceEmbedding.lean` exhibits the
blowup `X = Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)` of `Spec R` in `I` as a closed subscheme
`r : X ⟶ 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R} = Proj R[T₀, …, T_{m-1}]` over `Spec R`. This file computes, along `r`,
the twists of `X` and the two sheaves attached to its exceptional divisor `E`, the inverse image
of the centre:

* `𝒪_X(d) = r^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}}(d)` for every `d`;
* `𝒪_X(E) = 𝒪_X(-1)`;
* `𝒞_{E/X} = (r|_E)^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}}(1)` and `𝒩_{E/X} = (r|_E)^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}}(-1)`, where `r|_E` is
  the restriction `E ⟶ X ⟶ 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}` of `r` to the exceptional divisor.

For a regular local ring of dimension two and its maximal ideal these are the inputs to parts (2)
and (3) of Stacks tag 0AGQ. The tag, all three parts for one closed immersion `r`, is
`Stacks.Blowup.exists_isClosedImmersion_blowUpSpec_maximalIdeal_exceptional_projectiveLine` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/RegularSurfaceProjectiveLine.lean`; part (1) is proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/ExceptionalProjectiveLine.lean`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpecToProjSpacePullbackTwistIso`: the comparison
  `r^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}}(d) ≅ 𝒪_X(d)`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.twistPicardClass`: the class of `𝒪_X(d)` in `Pic(X)`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.invertibleSheafComapToSpecIsoTwistingSheafNegOne`: the isomorphism
  `𝒪_X(E) ≅ 𝒪_X(-1)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.twistPicardClass_add`: the class of `𝒪_X(d)` is additive in `d`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.nonempty_invertibleSheaf_comap_toSpec_iso_twistingSheaf_neg_one`:
  **`𝒪_X(E) ≅ 𝒪_X(-1)`.**
* `Stacks.Blowup.nonempty_conormalSheaf_iso_pullback_twistingSheaf_one` and
  `Stacks.Blowup.nonempty_normalSheaf_iso_pullback_twistingSheaf_neg_one`: **the conormal and
  normal sheaves of the exceptional divisor are pulled back from `𝒪(1)` and `𝒪(-1)`.**

## Implementation notes

The twist comparison is Tag 01N1 part (3) in the named form
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjMapTwistDegreeSection.pullbackTwistIso`, whose hypotheses are
surjectivity of the graded homomorphism (`Stacks.Blowup.surjective_reesPresentation`) and
generation of the source in degree one over its degree-zero part
(`MvPolynomial.adjoin_homogeneousSubmodule_one_eq_top`).

`𝒪_X(E) ≅ 𝒪_X(-1)` is proved in the Picard group rather than by exhibiting a map. The ideal sheaf
`𝒪_X(-E) = ℐ_E` is `𝒪_X(1)` by `Stacks.Blowup.twistOneIsoExceptionalIdealSheafOfIdealTop`
(Tag 02OS part (3) for the affine model), the class of `𝒪_X(d)` is additive in `d` because the
Rees algebra is generated in degree one so Equation 01MO is an isomorphism
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistDegreeOneCover.twistMultiplicationIso`), and
`[𝒪_X(-D)] = -[𝒪_X(D)]` is `Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwistPicardClass_eq_neg`. So
`[𝒪_X(E)] = -[ℐ_E] = -[𝒪_X(1)] = [𝒪_X(-1)]`, and equality of classes of invertible modules is
isomorphism (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass_eq_iff`). The class of `𝒪_X(0)` is shown to
vanish from additivity alone — it is its own double — so no identification `𝒪_X(0) ≅ 𝒪_X` is
needed.

Part (3) is then Tag 0B3P: the conormal sheaf of a closed subscheme is the restriction of its
ideal sheaf (`Stacks.CartierConormal.conormalSheafIsoNegativeTwist`) and the normal sheaf of an
effective Cartier divisor is the restriction of `𝒪_X(D)`
(`Stacks.Divisors.normalSheafIsoInvertibleSheaf`), composed with the two isomorphisms above and
with `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp` to turn `i^*r^*` into `(i ≫ r)^*`.

The exceptional divisor is written out as

```
(Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
  (Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I)).comap (toSpec I)
```

which is the spelling in which
`Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_toSpec_ofIdealTop` and
`Stacks.Blowup.twistOneIsoExceptionalIdealSheafOfIdealTop` are stated, rather than abbreviated.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B3P](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B3P)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MO)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj (twistingSheaf)
open Stacks.RingedSpace (structureIsSheaf)

universe u

namespace Stacks.Blowup

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R)

/-! ### The twists are pulled back from projective space -/

/-- **The twists of the blowup are pulled back from projective space.** For the closed immersion
`r : X ⟶ 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}` of the blowup of `Spec R` in an ideal `I` generated by `m` elements,
the twist `𝒪_X(d)` of the blowup is the pullback `r^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}}(d)` of the twist of projective
space, for every `d`. At `d = -1` this is the second equality of part (2) of Stacks tag 0AGQ. -/
def blowUpSpecToProjSpacePullbackTwistIso {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R) (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I)
    (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) (d : ℤ) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback (blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan)).obj
        (twistingSheaf (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R) d) ≅
      twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) d :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjMapTwistDegreeSection.pullbackTwistIso
    (reesPresentation I x hx) _ (surjective_reesPresentation I x hx hspan)
    (MvPolynomial.adjoin_homogeneousSubmodule_one_eq_top (Fin m) R) d

/-! ### `𝒪_X(E) = 𝒪_X(-1)` -/

/-- The Picard class of the twist `𝒪_X(m)` on the affine blowup `X = Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)`. -/
abbrev twistPicardClass (m : ℤ) : Stacks.Picard.ofScheme (blowUpSpec I) :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass (blowUpSpec I).presheaf
    (structureIsSheaf (blowUpSpec I).toRingedSpace)
    (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) m) (isInvertible_blowUpTwist I m)

/-- **The Picard class of the twists of the affine blowup is additive in the degree**: the
multiplication map `𝒪_X(m) ⊗ 𝒪_X(m') ⟶ 𝒪_X(m + m')` of Equation 01MO is an isomorphism, because
the Rees algebra is generated in degree one over `R`. -/
theorem twistPicardClass_add (m m' : ℤ) :
    twistPicardClass I (m + m') = twistPicardClass I m + twistPicardClass I m' := by
  have hm : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (blowUpSpec I).presheaf
      (structureIsSheaf (blowUpSpec I).toRingedSpace) (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) m) :=
    isInvertible_blowUpTwist I m
  have hm' : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (blowUpSpec I).presheaf
      (structureIsSheaf (blowUpSpec I).toRingedSpace) (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) m') :=
    isInvertible_blowUpTwist I m'
  have htens := Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_tensorSheaf (blowUpSpec I).presheaf
    (structureIsSheaf (blowUpSpec I).toRingedSpace)
    (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) m) (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) m')
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass_tensorSheaf (blowUpSpec I).presheaf
    (structureIsSheaf (blowUpSpec I).toRingedSpace) (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) m)
    (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) m') hm hm' htens).symm
  refine (Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass_eq_iff (blowUpSpec I).presheaf
    (structureIsSheaf (blowUpSpec I).toRingedSpace) _ _
    (isInvertible_blowUpTwist I (m + m')) htens).2 ⟨?_⟩
  exact (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistDegreeOneCover.twistMultiplicationIso (reesGrading I)
    (iSup_basicOpen_reesGrading_one_eq_top I) m m').symm

/-- The Picard class of `𝒪_X(0)` vanishes: it is its own double. -/
theorem twistPicardClass_zero : twistPicardClass I 0 = 0 := by
  have h := twistPicardClass_add I 0 0
  rw [add_zero] at h
  exact left_eq_add.mp h

/-- The Picard class of `𝒪_X(-1)` is the negative of that of `𝒪_X(1)`. -/
theorem twistPicardClass_neg_one :
    twistPicardClass I (-1) = -twistPicardClass I 1 := by
  have h := twistPicardClass_add I 1 (-1)
  rw [add_neg_cancel, twistPicardClass_zero] at h
  exact (neg_eq_of_add_eq_zero_right h.symm).symm

/-- **`𝒪_X(E) ≅ 𝒪_X(-1)` for the affine blowup**, as a `Nonempty`. -/
theorem nonempty_invertibleSheaf_comap_toSpec_iso_twistingSheaf_neg_one :
    Nonempty (Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf'
        ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
            (Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I)).comap (toSpec I)) ≅
      twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) (-1)) := by
  have := isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_toSpec_ofIdealTop I
  have hneg : Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwistPicardClass
      ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I)).comap (toSpec I)) =
      twistPicardClass I 1 :=
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass_eq_iff (blowUpSpec I).presheaf
      (structureIsSheaf (blowUpSpec I).toRingedSpace) _
      (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) 1)
      (Stacks.Divisors.isInvertible_negativeTwist_picard _)
      (isInvertible_blowUpTwist I 1)).2
      ⟨(twistOneIsoExceptionalIdealSheafOfIdealTop I).symm⟩
  have hpos : Stacks.Divisors.picardClass
      ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I)).comap (toSpec I)) =
      twistPicardClass I (-1) := by
    rw [twistPicardClass_neg_one, ← hneg, Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwistPicardClass_eq_neg, neg_neg]
  exact (Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass_eq_iff (blowUpSpec I).presheaf
    (structureIsSheaf (blowUpSpec I).toRingedSpace) _ _
    (Stacks.Divisors.isInvertible_invertibleSheaf_picard _)
    (isInvertible_blowUpTwist I (-1))).1 hpos

/-- **`𝒪_X(E) ≅ 𝒪_X(-1)` for the affine blowup.** The invertible sheaf `𝒪_X(E)` of the
exceptional divisor of the blowup of `Spec R` in an ideal `I` is the twist `𝒪_X(-1)`, the first
equality of part (2) of Stacks tag 0AGQ. -/
def invertibleSheafComapToSpecIsoTwistingSheafNegOne :
    Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf'
        ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
            (Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I)).comap (toSpec I)) ≅
      twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) (-1) :=
  (nonempty_invertibleSheaf_comap_toSpec_iso_twistingSheaf_neg_one I).some

/-! ### The conormal and normal sheaves of the exceptional divisor -/

/-- **The conormal sheaf of the exceptional divisor is pulled back from `𝒪(1)`.** The conormal
sheaf
`𝒞_{E/X}` of the exceptional divisor is the pullback of `𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}}(1)` along the restriction
`E ⟶ X ⟶ 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}` of the closed immersion `r` to `E`. -/
theorem nonempty_conormalSheaf_iso_pullback_twistingSheaf_one {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R)
    (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I) (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) :
    Nonempty (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf
        ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
          (Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I)).comap
            (toSpec I)).subschemeι ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback
          (((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
            (Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I)).comap
              (toSpec I)).subschemeι ≫ blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan)).obj
        (twistingSheaf (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R) 1)) :=
  ⟨Stacks.CartierConormal.conormalSheafIsoNegativeTwist _ ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback _).mapIso
      ((twistOneIsoExceptionalIdealSheafOfIdealTop I).symm ≪≫
        (blowUpSpecToProjSpacePullbackTwistIso I x hx hspan 1).symm) ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp _ (blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan)).app _⟩

/-- **The normal sheaf of the exceptional divisor is pulled back from `𝒪(-1)`.** The normal
sheaf `𝒩_{E/X}` of
the exceptional divisor is the pullback of `𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}}(-1)` along the restriction
`E ⟶ X ⟶ 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}` of the closed immersion `r` to `E`. -/
theorem nonempty_normalSheaf_iso_pullback_twistingSheaf_neg_one {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R)
    (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I) (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) :
    Nonempty (Stacks.Divisors.normalSheaf
        ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
          (Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I)).comap
            (toSpec I)).subschemeι ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback
          (((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
            (Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I)).comap
              (toSpec I)).subschemeι ≫ blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan)).obj
        (twistingSheaf (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R) (-1))) := by
  have := isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_toSpec_ofIdealTop I
  exact ⟨Stacks.Divisors.normalSheafIsoInvertibleSheaf _ ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback _).mapIso
      (invertibleSheafComapToSpecIsoTwistingSheafNegOne I ≪≫
        (blowUpSpecToProjSpacePullbackTwistIso I x hx hspan (-1)).symm) ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp _ (blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan)).app _⟩

end Stacks.Blowup

end
